---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PayoffCalculator from '../../components/PayoffCalculator';
const title='Student Loan Payoff & Extra Payment Calculator';
const description='Compare fixed-rate student loan payoff time, total interest and monthly or annual amortization schedules with and without extra payments.';
---
<Base {title} {description} kind="WebApplication" og="payoff">
 <header class="hero tool-detail-hero page-hero">
  <a class="tool-back" href="/tools/">← All planning tools</a>
  <span class="eyebrow page-hero-kicker">Interactive planning tool</span>
  <h1>{title}</h1>
  <p>{description}</p>
  <a class="primary button-link tool-start" href="#payoff-workspace">Use this tool <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
 </header>
 <PayoffCalculator client:load />
 <section class="support page-section">
 <h2>How extra payments affect a fixed-rate payoff estimate</h2>
 <p>This tool compares two otherwise identical monthly amortization schedules. It estimates a level payment from the balance, annual rate divided by 12 and remaining months. Each period's interest is calculated on the remaining principal; payment above interest reduces principal. It assumes no changes to the rate or scheduled payment.</p>
 <h2>When is the comparison useful?</h2>
 <p>Use it for hypothetical fixed-rate scenarios. It is not an income-driven repayment or forgiveness simulator. If you have federal loans, check your actual terms, payment allocation and any benefits before changing payments. Federal student loans generally accrue interest daily; this monthly model may differ from a servicer's payoff quote.</p>
 <p>Read <a href="/guides/student-loan-interest-explained/">how student loan interest works</a>, compare <a href="/calculator/">federal repayment plans</a>, or visit <a href="https://studentaid.gov/manage-loans/repayment">Federal Student Aid's repayment guidance</a>.</p>
 </section>
</Base>
